cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: AeroFlux
abstract: >-
  A zero-dependency, zero-heap, deterministic 3D incompressible
  Navier-Stokes solver in Go, with a hardware-accelerated data plane on
  Apple Silicon via the Accelerate framework. Fluid state is held in an
  off-heap mmap arena flanked by PROT_NONE guard pages; the timestep hot
  path performs no Go heap allocation, and results are bit-for-bit
  reproducible independent of worker count. Uses a staggered
  Marker-and-Cell grid, semi-Lagrangian advection, symmetric Strang
  splitting, and a pressure projection solved either by Red-Black
  Gauss-Seidel or by a prefactorized Cholesky decomposition through
  Accelerate's sparse solvers.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Saini
    given-names: Eklavya
